  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nHigh temperatures on Monday will warm a few more degrees. This\nwill be followed by a cooling trend for Tuesday through Thursday\nwith Thursday high temperatures in the upper 60s to mid 70s for\nthe coast and valleys, in the 50s to mid 60s for the mountains,\nand in the lower 80s for the lower deserts.\n\nThere could be some light showers as early as Thursday as a lower\nlatitude low pressure system moving across the eastern Pacific\nmoves closer to the West Coast.\n\nNBM chances for 0.01 inch or more of rainfall for the coast to the\nmountains increases from 10 to 20 percent for next Friday to 35 \nto 45 percent on Saturday the 31st to 40 to 50 percent on Sunday \nNovember 1st.",
